# Attenuator scenario file
# syntax: 
# section <name> to define a scenario
# 	  CH<ATTENUATOR_PORT> = (<X_VALUE>,<DAMPING_VALUE>)
#	  damping values are interpolated between given steps;
#	  e.g. (1,10) (10,1)  will be intepolated to:
#	  (1,10) (2,9) (3,8) (4,7) (5,6) (6,5) (7,4) (8,3) (9,2) (10,1)
#	  possible damping values depend on used attenuator
#	  attenuator control is done via taf.attenuator.set_attenuation KW
#	  attenuator is defined in __init__.py
#	  taf library + attenuator setup has to be done in robot TC
#
#	  example section: handover from channel1 to channel2
#
section test
	CH1	=	(1,10) (10,31) (20,31) (30,55)
	CH2	=	(1,55) (30,10)

# corresponding robot TC would look like:
#
#
#	*** Settings ***
#	Resource    ../attenuator_scenario.robot
#	Library         taf.hw.rf_attenuator               WITH NAME    attenuator
#	*** Test Cases ***
#	scenario_test
#		${attenuator}=    attenuator.setup_attenuator    attenuator=${tl.attenuators[${1}]}    alias=attenuator
#		run attenuator scenario  att=attenuator    att_file=${CURDIR}/attenuator_scenario.txt    scenario=test
